#!/bin/sh /etc/rc.common
# Additional configuration for the external gigabit PHY on port 0.
#
# WHY IS THIS NEEDED?
#
# For HH71VM, the only RJ45 is connected not to the built-in (100-megabit) ports SoC, but to
# EXTERNAL gigabit PHY: port 0 of the switch operates in GMII mode, PHY sits at MDIO address 6
# (in the driver - PORT0_RGMII_PHYID, AsicDriver/rtl865x_asicL2.h).
#
# ROM - this loader PHY configures itself - can be seen in its output with the command ETH
# ("Auto PHYID=0x6, page=0xd08, regID=0x11, read back data=0x9" etc.), and that's why
# TFTP - image filling works. But the driver pulls the reset line PHY during initialization
# (branch CONFIG_RTL_8211F_SUPPORT), and the setting is lost.
#
# The symptom without this script is ONE WAY communication: the device receives packets (sees
# ARP requests, teaches MAC), and its own packets do not reach the other side.
#
# The stock firmware does exactly the same thing and for the same reason - in its log after
# "init started" comes the block "set phyReg fro Gigabit adapter" with the same three entries.
# The values ​​are taken verbatim from the drain log on this device instance.
#
# [UNSET] which of the three records is decisive: the third (register 0, value 0x1300)
# restarts autonegotiation, and it is possible that it alone is enough. Checked so far
# only using all three at once is like stock.
#
# It would be more correct to do this in the driver itself, immediately after resetting PHY. Left
# script, because that’s how the stock works and because it’s necessary to edit the vendor code for the sake of it
# at stage bring-up is redundant.

START=11

boot() {
	[ -e /proc/rtl865x/phyReg ] || return 0

	# PAD_CTRL_1 (0xb8000850) - mode and strength of pads RGMII port 0.
	#
	# The 25 (PAD_P0_RGMII_MODE) bit remains cleared after PHY is reset by the driver, and
	# the loader and drain keep it COCKED. With the bit reset, the port is formally
	# works and the link goes up, but the transfer router -> PC loses frames in
	# depending on their content: on random data 13-16% on gigabit
	# (8.9% on 100 Mbit), while any uniform pattern passes through cleanly.
	# Measured: with bit 0 - 5000 random frames, 780 lost from 2000 on
	# “killer” pair 2A CD; with bit 1 - 0 from 5000, and 5 MB to SSH go to 2.2 with
	# instead of 92 s. Analysis - docs/luci-overview-latency.md.
	#
	# The value is taken verbatim from the stock bootloader log on this instance
	# ("Write memory 0xb8000850 dat 0x6fca0030").
	[ -e /proc/rtl865x/memory ] && 		echo write 0xb8000850 0x6fca0030 > /proc/rtl865x/memory

	# page 0xd08 (3336) - adjustment of the analog part for this board
	echo extWrite 6 3336 17 0x9  > /proc/rtl865x/phyReg
	echo extWrite 6 3336 21 0x19 > /proc/rtl865x/phyReg
	# register 0 (BMCR): enable autonegotiation and restart it
	echo extWrite 6 0 0 0x1300   > /proc/rtl865x/phyReg
}
